  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "description": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "The **outbox** records order events in the database and a relay hands them to Kafka; **pending** and **oldest pending age** rise when Kafka is unreachable and fall to 0 when it drains (alert `OutboxStuck`). **Consumer lag** is records behind per group; **oldest in-flight record age** grows when a record keeps failing (alerts `ConsumerLagGrowing`, `PoisonRecordBlocked`). Series are reported by the apps themselves: a gap in a panel can mean the app is down (alert `AsyncMetricsMissing`). The per-event-type and per-group series appear only after the first event or consumer assignment (up to a minute). Panels group by `event_type` or `group`, never by order."
      }
    },
    {
